    <h1>Christopher Clarke</h1>
    <p class="subhead">Founder, The Web3 Family &middot; Creative Studio for Nonprofits &middot; Inglewood, California</p>

    <p>I help people who started a nonprofit after a full career in something else. You saw the need, you filed the paperwork, and you carry the whole mission in your head. I sit down with you, you talk, and I build while you watch. Every Friday, something exists that you can hand to somebody: a page you can text, a sheet you can leave on a table, or a video that says it once, well.</p>

    <h2>Why I do this</h2>
    <p>For fifteen years I did a version of this inside other companies. Somebody owned the work, somebody else owned the software, and I stood in the middle until that gap closed. Now I do it one person at a time, for the people doing good in their communities.</p>

    <h2>What I do</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Branding.</strong> Your logo, colors, and message, so people trust you on sight.</li>
        <li><strong>Content.</strong> Videos, flyers, decks, and posts, for screens and for print.</li>
        <li><strong>Websites.</strong> A home online, with a donation page that works on any phone.</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing.</strong> Getting the word out on social media, Google, YouTube, and email.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p>Everything lands in a Google Drive your organization owns, and it stacks up week after week.</p>

